    "q-16361": {
      "dom_id": "step-q16361",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x-3}-2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $-3$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $3$ units to the *right*, and\n\n- the $-2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *down*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264217/assets/b60c9c3b63c950e696f0a3e288bb95a9322c6e46d3d1bd0d813c08132b5e84e0.png)",
