      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x+2}+3?$",
      "worked_solution": "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $+2$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $2$ units to the *left*, and\n\n- the $+3$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $3$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264217/assets/0e1ce8d66a0b1f95750e76518bdcab86ff9613e3d5591f691346fa8b7ecdd68a.png)",
